## Usage Rules

1. **DESIGN.md** → Follow existing page blueprints when they match your feature. For new pages, propose changes consistent with the established design language.

2. **mvp-scope.md** → Do not implement features marked "out of scope" for MVP. If uncertain, check the explicit out-of-scope section first. Check the "Phase 2 Additions" section for feasibility-verified feature priorities from competitor demand analysis.

3. **tool-vision-and-market-research.md** → Align feature proposals with the AI-native vision (AI as default, not optional add-on) and credit-based monetization model.

4. **user-flows-ai-native.md** → Match existing user flow patterns before inventing new interaction models.

5. **Competitor intelligence** → Before proposing a feature that exists in Buffer/Hootsuite/Later, check the Buffer feature mapping for vote counts and feasibility status. If a feature is marked "NOT FEASIBLE via API", do not plan a full implementation — scope to what the platform APIs actually allow.

## Priority Order

MVP scope > Competitor feasibility > Design system > User flows > Vision. Scope boundaries and API constraints are the hard constraints; everything else is guidance.
